Subject: DEF: "Transhuman" - When coined?

In order to give proper credit for creation of one of our much-used terms,
"transhuman", I'd like to find exactly when it was coined.  Some months back,
I used the term in my Immortalist Philosophy column in CRYONICS, and was
taken to task by a reader for not crediting FM-2030 (then F.M. Esfandiary) for
inventing the term.  I replied that, though FM had certainly spread the term
around, he did not invent it.

I remember seeing the word used by T.H. Huxley, who lived from 1825 to 1895,
and so died the True Death before FM was born.  Huxley spelt it "Trans-human",
though no one hyphenates it now.  Can anyone tell me where Huxley used this
term, and what year it was?  Any Huxley scholars here?

I was surprised yesterday when I found the word actually defined in my Websters
Unabridged Dictionary:

TRANSHUMAN: a. superhuman

TRANSHUMANIZE: v.t.; transhumanized, pt., pp.; transhumanizing, p pr. to 
elevate or transform to something beyond what is human; to change from a 
human into a higher, purer, nobler, or celestial nature.


